implementationPlan.description:
GREEN in packages/moe-proxy/src/utils.ts, next to readDaemonInfoResult:
- const MAX_DAEMON_JSON_BYTES = 64 * 1024. Comment: daemon.json is repository content (a repository can commit one), and the cap matches the daemon and JetBrains readers. Wrapper RPCs spawn a fresh proxy per call, so the file is read again on every call.
- A private helper reads it bounded:
  - fs.openSync(filePath, 'r') and one Buffer.alloc(MAX + 1);
  - loop fs.readSync(fd, buf, total, buf.length - total, null) until it returns 0 or the buffer is full, since a device can return short reads;
  - fs.closeSync in finally;
  - return the UTF-8 text, or null when total > MAX.
- In readDaemonInfoResult, inside the existing try, replace fs.readFileSync(filePath, 'utf-8') with the helper. A null result returns { info: null, retryable: false, error: 'daemon.json is larger than 64 KiB' }.
- Error handling for IO errors stays as today, via the existing catch.

Keep the existsSync-missing retryable result, the shape check, the project comparison, index.ts and the README unchanged. Re-run step 1's tests in the snapshot: green.

Adversarial self-review (load adversarial-self-review) of the three-file diff. Check:
- the off-by-one at the cap;
- short reads are looped;
- the descriptor is closed on every path;
- no whole-file read of daemon.json is left (grep readFileSync in src);
- a missing file is still retryable within the reconnect window;
- the oversize error text carries no file content;
- the subprocess test kills its child and removes its temp dir even on failure;
- valid daemon.json files connect exactly as before.
Residuals, noted only and pre-existing:
- a daemon.json removed between existsSync and open is reported as invalid details (non-retryable), as today;
- opening a FIFO blocks, but git cannot commit FIFOs.
If the review changes bytes, re-run the step 3 gate fresh. Report the three paths in complete_step.modifiedFiles.
